          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اثبات کردن (esbât kardan) — \"to prove\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "او نمیتواند حرفش را اثبات کند. u nemitavânad harfash râ esbât konad. He cannot prove what he says."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Esbât \"proof\" + kardan. Formal; everyday speech prefers sâbet kardan. In Persian, ث sounds like s."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اثبات comes from Arabic ithbāt \"proving, establishing\" (EtymDB); Persian says the Arabic th as s. With kardan \"to do\" it becomes a verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
